- op: discuss  # 4b1d
  at: '2026-06-26T03:29:49Z'  # 4b1d
  by: agent  # 4b1d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4b1d
  clock: 4  # 4b1d
  nonce: 4b1d  # 4b1d
  message: "Fixed by dispatch:F7 (PR merged as 39cc8e6c3d). dead-code-maybe now consumes cross_language_hits as a DEMOTER: a candidate whose name appears in >= --cross-lang-threshold (default 3) other-language files is excluded from the dead set (near-certain cross-language dispatch / missing-edge FP, e.g. Lit *.render at CLH~94), and the count is reported as summary.demoted_cross_language. Behavioral evidence (production-path tests in test_cli_dead_code.py): test_demoter_excludes_at_threshold_1 asserts a CLH=1 candidate (ProcessPayment, name in a Python file) is NOT in dead_candidates and demoted_cross_language==1 when threshold=1; test_demoter_disabled_at_zero_keeps_candidate asserts threshold<=0 disables (candidate stays, count 0); test_default_threshold_keeps_low_clh asserts CLH=1 < default 3 is kept. WI-gavub recommended graded confidence-demotion (path 2) but no per-candidate dead-confidence score exists, so a thresholded hard exclusion (mirroring the dispatch_inherited_ids demoter) realizes the intent (low-CLH dead code preserved by threshold>1) at S effort."  # 4b1d
